// D1566 — arithmetic over an element of an UNPINNED `__array_new_default__` binding. The
// intrinsic's element is a hole until something pins it, and a hole nothing pins takes the
// `i32` default at the scope FLUSH (D1470) — after the body is checked. Every operator arm
// indexes `T.tys` with its operand's type, so the `-1` an open element reads back as was an
// out-of-bounds array access that TRAPPED the compiler: a wasm backtrace, exit 70, on a
// program whose `let a: i32[]` face already printed `1`.
// The probe stays because the ingredient is an operator over an element no annotation, store
// or push ever pinned, and no corpus cell has it. Found by the agent on #2496.
// Should print 1.
function f() {
  let a = __array_new_default__(3)
  print(a[0] + 1)
}
f()
